{#
    `.. hlist::` — short items an author asked to be read across.

    The count is a modifier rather than the core's separate `columns-N`: it is
    one thing at one of several widths, which is what `--` means everywhere
    else in this vocabulary. Written out rather than interpolated, because a
    class assembled from a value is a class no check can find — and the list
    is also what says which counts the component has.
#}
{%- set widths = { 3: 'sds-hlist--3', 4: 'sds-hlist--4', 5: 'sds-hlist--5', 6: 'sds-hlist--6' } -%}
<div class="sds-hlist{% if widths[node.option('columns')] is defined %} {{ widths[node.option('columns')] }}{% endif %}">
    {{ renderNode(node.value) }}
</div>
